[{"page":1,"text":"MINUTES OF A SPECIAL SESSION\n\nCITY COUNCIL MEETING\n\nFebruary 3, 2026, at 6:00 PM\n\nPresent\n\nMayor Zack Stratton\n\nCouncilmember Parker McCumber\n\nCouncilmember Jacob Wood\n\nCouncilmember Jacob Holdaway\n\nCouncilmember David Lauret\n\nCouncilmember Ezra Nair\n\nAbsent\n\nStaff Present: Chief Deputy Holden Rockwell with the Utah County Sheriff’s Office,\nAdministrative Director David Kyle Herring, Interim City Attorney Jesse Riddle, City Treasurer\n\nZack Adams, Public Works Director Naseem Ghandour, and Deputy Recorder Tony Lara\nOthers Speaking: Chris Harding with CPA Insight Solutions, Seth Oveson with the Utah State\n\nAuditor’s Office, Vineyard resident Karsten Walker.\n\n1.\n\nCALL TO ORDER/INVOCATION/INSPIRATIONAL THOUGHT/PLEDGE OF\n\nALLEGIANCE\n\nMayor Stratton called the meeting to order at 6:00pm Vineyard resident Karsten Walker\noffered a prayer and led the pledge of allegiance.\n\n2.\n\nPRESENTATIONS/RECOGNITIONS/AWARDS/PROCLAMATIONS\n\n2.1. Chris Harding Presentation\n\nChris Harding with CPA Insight Solutions explained work that he had done for the city in the\npast and presented potential work that the council has asked him to do. He broke down the costs and\nexpected work for several different possible projects.\nCouncil discussed the previous audit that Mr. Harding had performed. Additionally, they asked\nquestions about future work with the city as it related to his work proposals as well as the different\ntypes of audits he could perform and what the differences were between them. There was discussion\nregarding the benefits of performing a forensic audit.\nCouncilmember Nair asked if there had been any other bids for the additional audits and if any\nof them had been firms that specialize in forensic audits. A discussion ensued.\n\n3.\n\nWORK SESSION\n\nPage 1 of 3; February 3, 2026, City Council Minutes","ocr":false},{"page":2,"text":"3.1. State Auditor's Office Presentation and Question and Answer\n\nSeth Oveson with the State Auditor’s Office, presented, regarding concerns that had come to his\noffice from the city. They ranged from questions regarding GRAMA requests, release of the general\nledger, findings that had been provided to the city, and the process by which the city responded to\nthe audit findings.\nThe council thanked Mr. Oveson for his work and discussed the content of the presentation.\n\nThere were several clarifying questions asked by the council.\n\n4.\n\nPUBLIC COMMENTS\n\nThere were no comments from the public during this meeting.\n\n5.\n\nMAYOR AND COUNCILMEMBERS' REPORTS/DISCLOSURES/RECUSALS\n\n6.\n\nSTAFF, COMMISSION, AND COMMITTEE REPORTS\nCouncilmember Lauret gave an update on the work being done by the staffing subcommittee.\n\n7.\n\nCONSENT ITEMS\n\n7.1. Approval of the January 20th 2026, City Council Meeting Minutes\n\n7.2. Approval of the January 27th 2026 City Council Meeting Minutes\n\n7.3. City Council Annual Meeting Schedule Amendment #2 (Resolution 2026-08)\n\nMotion: COUNCILMEMBER HOLDAWAY MOVED TO PULL ITEM 7.3 FOR\n\nDISCUSSION AND APPROVE ITEMS 7.1 AND 7.2 AS PRESENTED. COUNCILMEMBER\n\nMCCUMBER SECONDED. MAYOR STRATTON AND COUNCILMEMBERS NAIR, LAURET,\n\nWOOD, HOLDAWAY, AND MCCUMBER VOTED IN FAVOR. THE MOTION PASSED\n\nUNANIMOUSLY.\nThe council discussed item 7.3. The decision was made to continue the item to the next week.\n\nMotion: COUNCILMEMBER NAIR MOVED TO CONTINUE ITEM 7.3.\n\nCOUNCILMEMBER LAURET SECONDED. MAYOR STRATTON AND\n\nCOUNCILMEMBERS NAIR, LAURET, WOOD, HOLDAWAY, AND MCCUMBER VOTED IN\n\nFAVOR. THE MOTION PASSED UNANIMOUSLY.\n\n8.\n\nAPPOINTMENTS/REMOVALS\n\n8.1. Appointment of City Recorder\n\nThis item was continued to a future meeting.\nPage 2 of 3; February 3, 2026, City Council Minutes","ocr":false},{"page":3,"text":"9.\n\nBUSINESS ITEMS\n\nThere were no business items in this meeting.\n\n10. CLOSED SESSION\n\nThere was no closed session held during this meeting.\n\n11. ADJOURNMENT\n\nThe meeting was adjourned at 8:04pm\n\nMINUTES APPROVED ON:\n\n2/10/2026\n\nCERTIFIED CORRECT BY:\n\nTONY LARA, DEPUTY CITY RECORDER\n\nPage 3 of 3; February 3, 2026, City Council Minutes","ocr":false}]